ademy/question-capture/13931905/assets/cb569d4b7b76699259d2167b8c930e636e3fb794b14ef25a4d909c224235d7c3.png)\n\nAny point $(x,y)$ on the unit circle is related to the central angle $\\theta $ as follows:\n\n$$\nx=cos⁡\\theta ,\\,y=sin⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nWe're given that $x=\\frac{3}{7}$ at the point $P.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\ncos⁡\\theta =\\frac{3}{7}.\n$$\n\nWe can use the Pythagorean identity to find $sin⁡\\theta :$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1 \\\\ {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ sin⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $cos⁡\\theta =\\frac{3}{7}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sin⁡\\theta  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-{(\\frac{3}{7})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{1-\\frac{9}{49}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{40}{49}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{2\\sqrt{10}}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we select the positive answer since $sin⁡\\theta $ is positive in the first quadrant. So our final answer is $sin⁡\\theta =\\frac{2\\sqrt{10}}{7}$" 13194139533658 true] [17592186244775 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244776 13194139533658 true] [17592186244775 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244777 13194139533658 true] [17592186244775 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244778 13194139533658 true] [17592186244775 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244779 13194139533658 true] [17592186244775 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244780 13194139533658 true] [17592186244775 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533658 true] [17592186244775 1041 "selection" 13194139533658 true] [17592186244775 1104 #edb/ref 17592186244779 13194139533658 true] [17592186244775 1110 #uuid "7c2731e8-6c66-5103-b8c7-b1f4cc1bd6c1" 13194139533658 true] [17592186244776 1034 "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{7}" 13194139533658 true] [17592186244776 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533658 true] [17592186244776 1111 #uuid "01346b90-c281-56d5-bbc9-27c0b953b25b" 13194139533658 true] [17592186244777 1034 "\\frac{4}{7}" 13194139533658 true] [17592186244777 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533658 true] [1759218